OpenWings patch 0002: keep deployment secrets out of third-party child processes

Upstream hands its full environment to user-added stdio MCP servers (whenever
they define any env var), to the bundled npx browser server and to Cookbook
serving commands. In OpenWings the launcher (wings/serve.py) already removes
ODYSSEUS_APP_KEY and ODYSSEUS_ADMIN_PASSWORD from the server's environment, so
no child inherits them; this patch additionally strips every secret-looking
variable (provider keys, OAuth client secrets, tokens) from the environment of
user-added MCP servers and Cookbook commands (wings/envscrub.py), and passes
the key explicitly only to upstream's own Python MCP servers (memory, rag,
email, image_gen), which need it to read encrypted credentials.

Applies to: odysseus-dev/odysseus@9d0d3720f4ca181d87bef94da826d730acc6d483
License: AGPL-3.0-or-later (same as upstream)

